              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for a broker, then the Hindi for to pay off."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: कमाना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कमाना — kamānā — \"to earn\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मेरा भाई दुकान से अच्छा पैसा कमाता है। merā bhāī dukān se acchā paisā kamātā hai. My brother earns good money from his shop."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने बहुत पैसा कमाया, usne bahut paisā kamāyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कमाना (kamānā) goes back to karmāpayati, \"works, earns\", a form CDIAL reconstructs (CDIAL 2897), built on karman, \"work\". कमाई, earnings, is its noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
